              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "linda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very refreshing. The mint used in juleps is called Corsican Mint. It has tiny leaves &amp; the plant grows as a ground cover - much different than peppermint and similar varieties. The flavor is very strong. I planted some this spring and have enjoyed it in tea, orange juice, and cocktails."
          },
